
a) Python program to display the given integer in reverse
num = int(input("Enter an integer: "))
rev = 0

while num > 0:
    digit = num % 10
    rev = rev * 10 + digit
    num = num // 10

print("Reversed number:", rev)


b) Python program to replace all occurrences of first character with '$' (except the first one)

s = input("Enter a string: ")

first_char = s[0]
modified = first_char + s[1:].replace(first_char, '$')

print("Modified string:", modified)


c) Python program to find the largest number in a list without built-in functions

numbers = [12, 45, 7, 23, 89, 5]

largest = numbers[0]

for num in numbers:
    if num > largest:
        largest = num

print("Largest number:", largest)